Subject: [PATCH 10747/11362] The operational retrospective never reports the
 quarantine rate

operational_retro_2026_09_601 summarises the milestone as 9 experiments in 5.0
minutes with three bottlenecks about telemetry and GPU reporting. Searching it for
flagged, quarantin, adversarial and duration_too_short returns zero occurrences.
The conductor logged 7 FLAGGED rows in the same window and 6 of 13 experiment
artifacts written today carry flagged_adversarial true.

So the mechanism that answers "how did this milestone go" reads as healthy while
about half the output was quarantined by the fabrication gate. The data was
available: those rows are in ops/conductor-log.md, which the retro path already
parses for timings, and flagged_adversarial appears nowhere in that code path.

The entry stresses that this is independent of the false-positive defect. Even if
all 7 flags were true positives, reporting 9 experiments completed without saying 7
were quarantined describes a different milestone than the one that happened. If the
flags are false the number is the tax; if they are true it is the finding. Silence
is wrong either way, so the fix does not wait on resolving the marker scan.

The step-6 candidate is small: the retro already reads the conductor log, so
counting FLAGGED, GATE_BLOCK and FAIL rows next to experiments_completed needs no
new data source and would have surfaced today's 46% without hand-counting. Not built
here because it changes the retro schema and existing consumers need checking.

Limits recorded: one milestone, one artifact. The claim is that this retro omitted
it and the code path has no flag reference, not that every past retro did.

